{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2138-12-21 20:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi Mr. ___, I'm Dr. ___. You're here tonight for your scheduled bronchoscopy to dilate your airway and replace your tracheostomy tube. How are you feeling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2138-12-21 20:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hey, doctor. I’m okay, a little nervous. My breathing’s been tighter lately, so I guess this is needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2138-12-21 20:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s understandable. The tightness is due to the tracheal stenosis from your Ruvalcaba-Myhre-Smith syndrome and relapsing polychondritis. The procedure tomorrow will help open it up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2138-12-21 20:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Right, we’ve done this before. But last time, the custom tube didn’t fit. Will that happen again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2138-12-21 20:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll assess during the procedure. If needed, we’ll use a standard tube like last time. The main goal is to dilate the trachea and bronchi safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2138-12-21 20:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And the pain afterward? Last time I needed oxycodone for a day or two."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2138-12-21 20:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll keep your pain meds available—acetaminophen, ibuprofen, and oxycodone as needed. You may feel some soreness at the trach site, but we’ll manage it well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2138-12-21 20:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. I’ll rest up tonight then."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2138-12-22 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re up early. How’d you sleep?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2138-12-22 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Not bad. A bit stiff, but I’m ready to get this done."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2138-12-22 08:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. The procedure is scheduled for 9 AM. We’ll dilate your trachea to 12 mm, right bronchus to 8 mm, and left to 10 mm. We’ll also take washings to check for infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2138-12-22 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I be out for it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2138-12-22 08:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’ll be under sedation. And afterward, you might be on the ventilator briefly just to help with pain control while you wake up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2138-12-22 08:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Like last time? That was weird, but okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2138-12-22 08:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’ll monitor you closely. Your vitals are stable now—heart rate 100, BP 99/55, oxygen at 99% on 40% trach mask."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2138-12-22 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. You’re back in your room. The procedure went well—no complications. We dilated as planned and replaced the trach tube."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2138-12-22 12:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I feel groggy. Was I on the vent?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2138-12-22 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, for about an hour. Just to help with pain while you came around. You’re now on the trach mask and breathing comfortably."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2138-12-22 12:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Any issues with the tube?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2138-12-22 12:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We used a standard Portex 9 again—the custom one didn’t fit due to compression. But it’s secure and working fine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2138-12-22 12:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Same as last time. Okay. How’s my breathing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2138-12-22 12:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Lungs are clear on exam. The chest X-ray shows no pneumothorax or fluid. Lung volumes were low earlier but improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2138-12-22 12:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the washings? Any sign of infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2138-12-22 12:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Sent to lab, but no results yet. We’ll follow up if anything comes back. Your white count is 13.6, a bit high, but that’s likely from inflammation, not infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2138-12-22 12:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. I’ve been on steroids for years—does that affect healing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2138-12-22 12:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It can slow tissue healing a bit, but we’re managing it. You’re still on your daily prednisone, and we’ll keep that consistent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2138-12-23 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. How’s the pain today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2138-12-23 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better. I took ibuprofen this morning and haven’t needed the oxycodone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2138-12-23 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great progress. We did another chest X-ray this morning—lungs are clear, no new issues. Cardiomegaly is stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2138-12-23 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I noticed some wheezing last night. Was that on the X-ray?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2138-12-23 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we heard some inspiratory wheezing, mostly on the right. Gave you one dose of IV decadron to reduce inflammation. It’s improved now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2138-12-23 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. So am I on track to go home tomorrow?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2138-12-23 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, if you keep doing this well. Pain controlled, breathing stable, no fever. We’ll plan for discharge tomorrow morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2138-12-23 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. What about my meds? Same as before?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2138-12-23 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes—continue all your home meds: inhaled tobramycin, fluticasone, losartan, pantoprazole, famotidine, pirfenidone, and your daily steroids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2138-12-23 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the oxycodone?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2138-12-23 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You can keep it for breakthrough pain, but only if needed. Most patients stop within a day or two."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2138-12-24 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Final check before discharge. You look great—sitting up, on your phone, breathing easy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2138-12-24 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Feeling good. No pain, no wheezing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2138-12-24 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Labs this morning are stable—WBC still 13.6, but that’s expected. No signs of infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2138-12-24 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I’m really going home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2138-12-24 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. You’ll go home today. Continue all medications, and the Interventional Pulmonary team will call to schedule your next dilation in a few weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2138-12-24 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And follow-up with rheumatology?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2138-12-24 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, they’re aware. Your relapsing polychondritis is well-managed, but we’ll keep monitoring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2138-12-24 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks, doc. I appreciate everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2138-12-24 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and call if you have trouble breathing or increased pain."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2138-12-21 20:27:00",
    "admission_end": "2138-12-24 12:45:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "Mr. ___ was admitted for a scheduled bronchoscopy with balloon dilation of the trachea and mainstem bronchi, along with tracheostomy tube exchange, due to recurrent tracheobronchial stenosis from Ruvalcaba-Myhre-Smith syndrome and relapsing polychondritis. The procedure was performed without complications, with successful dilation to 12 mm in the trachea, 8 mm in the right bronchus, and 10 mm in the left. A standard Portex 9 tracheostomy tube was placed due to compression preventing use of a custom tube. Post-procedure, he experienced mild pain managed with acetaminophen, ibuprofen, and oxycodone, and was briefly ventilated for analgesia. He developed mild wheezing on hospital day two, treated with a single dose of IV decadron. He remained stable, with clear lungs on imaging and no signs of infection. He was discharged home on day three with all home medications continued and follow-up planned with interventional pulmonary and rheumatology.",
    "problems": [
      "Other specified diseases of upper respiratory tract",
      "Ruvalcaba-Myhre-Smith syndrome",
      "Other specified disorders of cartilage, unspecified sites",
      "Tracheostomy status",
      "Other diseases of pharynx",
      "Gastro-esophageal reflux disease without esophagitis",
      "Essential (primary) hypertension"
    ]
  }
}
